defaultObjs
===========

Pyxplot's built-in namespace: the functions, constants, modules and physical
units which are available when Pyxplot starts. defaultVars.c puts them all into
the default namespace.

airyFuncs.c, airyFuncs.h
    The Airy functions Ai and Bi and their derivatives for complex arguments,
    which GSL does not provide. Provided courtesy of Matthew Smith.

defaultFuncs.c, defaultFuncs.h
    The built-in mathematical, string and utility functions, e.g. sin(),
    besselJ(), gcd(), len(), max() and eval().

defaultFuncsChecks.h
    Helper functions which built-in functions use to check their arguments
    (e.g. that they are real, dimensionless or integers) and to report errors
    in a consistent way.

defaultUnits.c, defaultUnits.h
    The database of physical units, with their names, dimensions, conversion
    factors, allowed SI prefixes and unit schemes. It is used to parse units in
    expressions and to choose units in which to display results.

defaultVars.c, defaultVars.h
    Builds the default namespace when Pyxplot starts: the constants, the
    built-in functions with their help text and LaTeX forms, and the modules.

moduleAst.c, moduleAst.h
    The ast module: cosmological distances, ages and redshifts, the sidereal
    time, and the phase of the Moon.

moduleColor.c, moduleColor.h
    The colors module's wavelength() and spectrum() functions, which compute the
    color the eye sees for monochromatic light or for a spectrum.

moduleFractals.c, moduleFractals.h
    The fractals module's julia() and mandelbrot() functions, for drawing images
    of these sets with the colormap plot style.

moduleOs.c, moduleOs.h
    The os module, which gives scripts access to the operating system: the
    environment, running shell commands, listing files, and the os.path
    functions.

modulePhy.c, modulePhy.h
    The phy module's black-body functions Bv() and Bvmax(); the physical
    constants in this module are set up in defaultVars.c.

moduleRandom.c, moduleRandom.h
    The random module, which draws random numbers from various distributions
    using GSL's random number generator.

moduleStats.c, moduleStats.h
    The stats module: probability density functions and cumulative distribution
    functions of common statistical distributions, and their inverses.

moduleTime.c, moduleTime.h
    The time module: functions which create date objects, measure the intervals
    between them, and format them as strings.

physConstants.h
    The physical constants used by the phy module and the unit database, from
    CODATA 2022 and the IAU's nominal values.

zetaRiemann.c, zetaRiemann.h
    The Riemann zeta function for complex arguments, which GSL does not
    provide. Provided courtesy of Matthew Smith.
